      "textEn": "250\nIn the Naimisharanya, inviting Yamraj to participate in the Yagya that was being completed. It was good for those\nwho did not want to die. That which is not touched by anyone, that which is always there, is the end of all.\nFor this reason, the Lord has spoken, the supreme sages.\nOh, in this world, the nectar of the play of Hari is not drunk by humans. 8 ”. Meaning of the word:\nNa- not; Kashit- to whom; Priyate- to be dear; Tavat- until; Yavat- up to; Aaste- are present; Iha- this; Antakah- after that;\nThose who end the life; Tad- this; Artham- reason; Hi- certainly; Bhagavan- representative of God; Aahutah- invited; Para- great; Rishibhih- by the great sages; Aho- oh; Nri- in human society; Piyetah- let (someone) drink; Harilila- divine plays of God; Amritam- nectar; Vachah- what;\nUntil the death of the son of the earth, Yamraj is present here, until then no one's death\nwill happen. The sages have invited Yama, the controller of death, who is the representative of the Lord.\nAll the creatures who come into their grasp should take advantage of this form of the divine plays of God, to listen to the nectar of immortality. Meaning: Every human wants that he should not die, but he does not know how to get rid of death. The elixir to escape death is the nectar-like play of God, to accustom oneself to listen to those, which are said in the Srimad Bhagavat in a sequential manner.\nTherefore, here it is advised that any man who desires to be free from death,\nshould adopt the lifestyle prescribed by the sages like Shaunaka.\nMandaasyam mandaaprajnasyam vayo mandaayushascha vai.\nNidraaya hiyeate naktam diva cha vyarthakarmabhih. 9>. Meaning of the word:\nOf the lazy; slow; of the intellect; age; slow; ATW: of age; also; and; Vai:\nApproximately; in sleep; passes; night; day; also; vain; by actions;\nHL"
