      "textEn": "252\n\nMeaning of the word:\nSoota said: Suta Goswami said; Yada--When; Parikshit- Maharaja Parikshit; Kuru- Jadgali-- The capital of Kuru country;\nAvasat- used to live; Kali- the characteristics of Kali Yuga; Praveshitam- entered; Nija- in one's own limits; Nishamy- not very interesting; Tatha- thereafter; Sharasanam- bow and arrow;\nSanyuga- having the opportunity; Shaundi- heroic deed; Adade- having accepted L\n\nSoota Goswami said: When Maharaja Parikshit was living in the capital of the Kuru Empire,\nhe saw the signs of Kali Yuga entering within the borders of his kingdom. When he found out about this,\nhe did not find it interesting. But this gave him the opportunity to fight against it\ncertainly. Therefore, he picked up his bow and arrow and became ready for military action. Meaning: The governance of Maharaja Parikshit was so efficient that he was living peacefully in his capital.\nBut they received news that the signs of Kali Yuga had entered their kingdom's borders,\nand they did not like this news. What are the characteristics of Kali Yuga? 2. These are as follows:\n(1) Illicit relationships with women, (2) addiction to meat-eating, (3) intoxication (intoxication),\nand (4) interest in gambling. The literal meaning of Kali Yuga is the age of strife, and in human society,\nthe above four characteristics are the main causes of all kinds of strife. ©. Maharaj Parikshit heard that some people in his\nkingdom had already fallen victim to those characteristics, so he wanted to take immediate action against such causes of unrest. This means that at least until the reign of Maharaja\nParikshit, such characteristics in public life were practically unknown, and as soon as\nthey were discovered, they wanted to completely destroy them. This news did not seem interesting to him,\nbut from one perspective, Maharaj Parikshit was getting this opportunity to fight.\nAlthough small-\nThere was no need to fight small states, because they were all peacefully under their control, but\nThe wicked of Kali Yuga gave them the opportunity to show their bravery. A true Kshatriya,\nAs soon as he gets the opportunity to fight, he becomes elated, just as when an opportunity to play a game arises,\nthe player becomes eager. It is no argument that such characteristics are predetermined in Kali Yuga.\nIf that were the case, then what was the need to attack against such characteristics? Such arguments"
