ternally\nexisting and never separate from them. These are (1) truthfulness (2) cleanliness (3) second,\nNot being able to bear the suffering of others, (4) the power to control anger, (5) self-satisfaction,\n(6 ) impartiality, (7 ) stability of mind, (8 ) restraint of desires, (9 ) responsibility,\n(10 ) equanimity, (19 ) tolerance, (12 ) equanimity, (93 ) obedience, (14 ) knowledge,\n(15 ) detachment from sensual pleasures, (16 ) leadership, (17) bravery, (18 ) effect,\n(19 ) making the impossible possible, (Ro) dutifulness, (21) complete freedom, (22 ) work,\n(23) beauty, (24) patience, (25) Compassion, (26) Generosity, (27) Humility,\n(28) Virtue, (29) Resolve, (30) Completeness of knowledge, (31) Appropriate skill, (32) All\nOwnership of worldly pleasures, ( 33 ) joy, ( 34 ) stability, ( 35 ) obedience, ( 36 ) glory,\n( 37 ) worship, ( 38 ) humility, ( 39 ) existence ( as God ), ( 40 ) purity. The complete, embodiment of all virtues and beauty, the supreme Lord, Shri Krishna, has stopped his divine\nleelas (divine plays) on this earth. In their absence, Kali has spread its influence everywhere. Therefore, seeing this state of the world, I am extremely sad."
